* 2611.00893's Problem asks which groups have ω_α(G) a subgroup for every involutory α: A₄ with conjugation by (12)
  gives |ω_α| = 6, not a subgroup (our check); an example, not a counterexample.
* No counterexample: 2611.05196 (cubic-partition congruences mod p^2α, α = 2), 2611.03879 (Graffiti #643, random graphs
  n ≤ 80), 2611.03403 (cube cycle constant, five vertices), 2611.05154 and 2611.05014 (not finitely testable / proved).
